1
00:05:18,947 --> 00:05:24,947
In a town with no justice, there is only one law... Every man for himself.

2
00:10:37,894 --> 00:10:43,894
Last Man Standing is a crime, action, western film directed by Walter Hill.

3
00:15:56,842 --> 00:16:02,842
John Smith is a mysterious stranger who is drawn into a
vicious war between two Prohibition-era gangs.

4
00:21:15,789 --> 00:21:21,789
In a dangerous game, he switches allegiances from one to
another, offering his services to the highest bidder.

5
00:26:34,736 --> 00:26:40,736
As the death toll mounts, Smith takes the law into his
own hands in a deadly race to stay alive.

6
00:31:53,684 --> 00:31:59,684
John Smith, played by Bruce Willis.

7
00:37:12,631 --> 00:37:18,631
Sheriff Ed Galt, played by Bruce Dern.

8
00:42:31,578 --> 00:42:37,578
Joe Monday, played by William Sanderson.

9
00:47:50,526 --> 00:47:56,526
Hickey, played by Christopher Walken.

10
00:53:09,473 --> 00:53:15,473
Doyle, played by David Patrick Kelly.

11
00:58:28,421 --> 00:58:34,421
Felina, played by Karina Lombard.

12
01:03:47,368 --> 01:03:53,368
Last Man Standing is a 1996 American neo-Western action film
written, produced and directed by Walter Hill.

13
01:09:06,315 --> 01:09:12,315
It stars Bruce Willis, Christopher Walken and Bruce Dern.

14
01:14:25,263 --> 01:14:31,263
The film is a remake of the 1961 Japanese film Yojimbo by Akira
Kurosawa, relocated to the Prohibition-era American South.

15
01:19:44,210 --> 01:19:50,210
In the film, a mysterious gunman (Willis) arrives in a small town ruled by
rivaling gangs, and sets up about playing them against each other.

16
01:25:03,157 --> 01:25:09,157
The film was released by New Line Cinema on September 20, 1996.

17
01:30:22,105 --> 01:30:28,105
It received mixed reviews and was a commercial disappointment.

18
01:35:41,052 --> 01:35:47,052
The film explores themes of prohibition era,
texas, gang war, whiskey, on the run.
